{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "12", "m": "09", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "11", "M": "46", "S": "02"}}, "news": [{"title": "Nashik civic body to hold ward camps to bring 20,000 properties under tax net", "para": "Nashik Municipal Corporation will begin hosting targeted camps across various wards in October. These efforts are aimed at locating and evaluating unassessed properties, with expectations of including around twenty thousand new entries into the tax register. The initiative anticipates an additional fifteen crore rupees in annual income, as the corporation aims for a more robust property tax collection by 2026-27.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/nashik-civic-body-to-hold-ward-camps-to-bring-20000-properties-under-tax-net/134113824?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-216186/134113824.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Major relief for plot holders in Haryana as HSVP launches scheme to settle dues", "para": "Haryana Shehri Vikas Pradhikaran has launched the Vivadon Se Samadhan Scheme 2026, presenting plot holders with a valuable opportunity to settle. This initiative aims to relieve over Rs 724 crore and will aid around 4,414 allottees from ten states. It encompasses residential, institutional, group housing, and industrial plots. Allottees are required to clear their dues by December 31, 2026, to avoid plot resumption.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/major-relief-for-plot-holders-in-haryana-as-hsvp-launches-scheme-to-settle-dues/134113755?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-69900/134113755.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Ahmedabad civic body, Auda fail to enforce structural stability certificate rule", "para": "Authorities in Ahmedabad are overlooking a significant requirement concerning older buildings, specifically the need for structural stability certificates for those over fifteen years old. While the state approved this regulation back in 2014, it has not been enforced. Insufficient staffing has been identified as a primary reason for the ongoing failure to implement this vital safety measure effectively.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/ahmedabad-civic-body-auda-fail-to-enforce-structural-stability-certificate-rule/134113684?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-241304/134113684.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}]}